Package: dsOMOP
Type: Package
Title: DataSHIELD Server-Side Integration for OMOP CDM Databases
Version: 2.5.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("David", "Sarrat González", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "david.sarrat@isglobal.org"),
    person("Xavier", "Escribà-Montagut", role = "aut"),
    person("Juan R", "González", role = "aut"))
Description: Server-side DataSHIELD package providing typed, reviewed access to
    OMOP Common Data Model databases. It uses vendored OHDSI CDM metadata, with
    optional CommonDataModel metadata, for schema and concept-role
    classification. Features include a curated query library with 80 locally
    controlled SQL templates, selected pre-computed and live-computed Achilles
    analysis contracts, plan-based extraction with feature engineering, cohort
    management, and endpoint-specific controls informed by DataSHIELD nfilter
    settings. Disclosure safety still depends on the deployed method allowlist,
    server policy, database privileges, and the contract of each operation.
    Includes DBI/ODBC resource connectors for PostgreSQL, SQLite, DuckDB,
    MySQL/MariaDB, SQL Server/Synapse/PDW, Oracle, Redshift, BigQuery,
    Snowflake, Spark, and Databricks, plus a small built-in SQL helper for
    parameter rendering, common DATEADD/DATEDIFF/TOP translations, and Oracle
    alias syntax. Canonical OHDSI
    SQL can optionally be rendered and translated with OHDSI SqlRender on its
    supported dialects; MySQL/MariaDB remain an explicitly reviewed extension.
    Query feature parity depends on the target DBMS and installed driver.
